   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI_06">Seefeldstrasse 73</name> <hi rend="underline">
                                    <hi rend="superscript">III</hi>
                                </hi>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zurich</name> VIII: <name type="geo" key="G_CHE">Switzerland</name>
                            </addrLine> </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear Miss <name type="person" key="weav76">Weaver</name>: Many thanks for <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">letter</seg> and <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">enclosures</seg>. Am sorry to hear the <seg xml:id="seg3" type="note-anchor">sales</seg> are unsatisfactory and hope they will improve. You do not say if you have sent me <seg xml:id="seg4" type="note-anchor">the other dozen copies</seg> I wrote for. I am much better now but must remain for a fortnight still under doctor’s care. I am writing <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">
                            <hi rend="underline">Ulysses</hi>
                        </name> but as usual very slowly.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>        	With kind regards and thanks</salute>
                        <salute>                    	sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>                                	<name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1917-03-22">22.III.917</date>
                        </dateline> </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Harriet Weaver’s letter of <date when="1917-03-16">16 March 1917</date> (Firth 170).</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">Receipt for JJ’s money order for £2.6.4 and press notices for <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name> (Firth 170).</note>
                <note xml:id="note3" target="#seg3" type="commentary">In her letter to JJ of <date when="1917-03-16">16 March 1917</date>, Harriet Weaver wrote: “The sales have dropped off this week” (Firth 170).</note>
                <note xml:id="note4" target="#seg4" type="commentary">Copies of <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>. See <rs type="letter" key="L_71451">JJ to Weaver, <date when="1917-02-15">15 February 1917</date>
                    </rs>.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
